              ext_lo - Set IF external-LO (DBBC3 racks)

  Syntax:   ext_lo=loX,freq,sb,lo_min,lo_max,lo_sb
            ext_lo=
            ext_lo=loX
            ext_lo=all

  Response: ext_lo/loX,freq,sb,lo_min,lo_max,lo_sb

Settable parameters:

  loX       LO (IF) for this external-LO: 'loa', 'lob', ..., up to the last IF
            in the system ('loh' is the last possible) or 'all'. The default
            is 'all'. No previous value ('*') available.

  freq      External-LO frequency for this IF, MHz. Must be positive. No
            default. No previous value ('*') available.

  sb        External-LO side-band for this channel, 'usb' or 'lsb'. No
            default. No previous value ('*') available.

  lo_min    Minimum net-LO frequency (from 'lo=...) that this external-LO
            applies to. Must be non-negative. Default is no minimum. No
            previous value ('*') available.

  lo_max    Maximum net-LO frequency (from 'lo=...) that this external-LO
            applies to. Can't be set if 'lo_min' is not set. If set, must be
            non-negative and greater than or equal to 'lo_min'. Default is
            'lo_min' for an effective single frequency (or no maximum if
            'lo_min' is not set). No previous value ('*') available. See
            Comments for more details.

  lo_sb     net-LO side-band (from 'lo=...) that this external-LO applies to,
            'usb', 'lsb', or 'all'. Default is 'all'. No previous value ('*')
            available.

Monitor-only Parameters: None.

Comments:

This command specifies the effective total external-LO, before the DBBC3, for
a given IF. (The net-LO before the BBCs is still given by the 'lo=...'
commands.) This command does not set the external-LO; it just describes what
is expected. The external-LO table is used by the 'synth_mode=...' command to
calculate the synthesizer frequency needed to achieve the net-LO if the
corresponding 'ifX' input is '2'.

Before defining the external-LOs in the mode setup, an initial,'ext_lo=' (no
parameters) should be used to delete any previous defined entries. The
external-LO definition usually occurs before the 'synth_mode=...' commands in
the 'dbbc3_synth' local procedure.

Generally speaking, it is recommended to make the 'lo_min', 'lo_max', and
'lo_sb' parameters as restrictive as possible to reduce the risk of having a
table entry apply when it is not wanted.

Using 'all' for the IF is recommended in case the IF the signal goes to
change; this also reduces the number of table entries for dual polarization
modes. A maximum of 40 table entries are supported. Multiple table entries
for a given external-LO can used if necessary.

There are three options for 'lo_min' and 'lo_max': (i) both both are null for
no restriction based on frequency, (ii) 'lo_min' is non-negative and 'lo_max'
is null to select a single frequency, and (iii) 'lo_min' and 'lo_max' are
non-negative and 'lo_min' is less than equal to 'lo_max' to select a range (a
single frequency if 'lo_min' equals 'lo_max').

If 'lo_sb' is null or 'all', it applies to a net-LO of either side-band.

The monitor form 'ext_lo' will print the entire table. Using 'ext_lo=loX,?'
will show all entries that could potentially apply to that LO (IF). Using
'ext_lo=loX' with no additional parameters will show the table entry that
currently applies for that IF (or all IFs for 'ext_lo=all',in which case all
are shown in ascending IF order). These forms can be useful for debugging the
table. (When debugging, it may be necessary to remove old table entries with
'ext_lo=' before trying new entries: existing entries take precedence over new
entries.) The output is all null parameters if none apply, including if the LO
is not defined.

The external-LOs can be defined explicitly by IF. For example:

    ext_lo=
    ext_lo=loa,10000,usb
    ext_lo=lob,20000,lsb

For more complicated situations, a table of external-LO values that apply
depending on the net-LO for the IF can be used. The goal, when it is possible,
is to allow stations to specify a table, in the local 'dbbc3_synth' SNAP
procedure, that does not need to be revised depending on which input signal is
connected, and where. For example:

    ext_lo=
    ext_lo=all,10000,usb,15000,16000
    ext_lo=all,20000,usb,25000,26600

The above two statements would specify 10000 as the external-LO for any IF if
the net-LO frequency is between 15000 and 16000 and 20000 otherwise if between
25000 and 26000.

Multiple table entries may cover a given net-LO. The first in the table that
matches applies. Therefore you should enter the table with the most restrictive
entries before less restrictive ones. For example:

    ext_lo=
    ext_lo=all,10500,usb,20000,20000
    ext_lo=all,11000,usb,19000,21000

The following is an example of the LO configuration for a tri-band
dual-polarization configuration:

  The contents of 'ifdXX' and 'dbbc3_synth' procedures that are called from
  the 'setupXX' procedure are shown. The 'setupXX' and ifdXX' procedures are
  generated by 'drudg'. The 'dbbc3_synth' procedure is a station procedure and
  is in principle independent of the mode.

  ifdXX:

    ifa=1,agc,32000
    ifb=1,agc,32000
    ifc=2,agc,32000
    ifd=2,agc,32000
    ife=2,agc,32000
    iff=2,agc,32000
    lo=
    lo=loa,20400.00,usb,lcp,10.000
    lo=lob,20400.00,usb,rcp,10.000
    lo=loc,45800.00,lsb,lcp,10.000
    lo=lod,45800.00,lsb,rcp,10.000
    lo=loe,84700.00,usb,lcp,10.000
    lo=lof,84700.00,usb,rcp,10.000
    dbbc3_synth


  dbbc3_synth:

    ext_lo=
    ext_lo=all,20400,usb,20400,,usb
    ext_lo=all,38100,usb,45800,,lsb
    ext_lo=all,92400,lsb,84700,,usb
    synth_mode=
    synth_mode=loa,,,check
    synth_mode=lob,,,check
    synth_mode=loc,,,check
    synth_mode=lod,,,check
    synth_mode=loe,,,check
    synth_mode=lof,,,check

  The result of the 'synth_mode' commands is:

    /synth_mode/loa,(7700),disable,(20400/usb),,15.0,CW,external,10,enable,disable,0,locked
    /synth_mode/lob,(7700),disable,(20400/usb),,15.0,CW,external,10,enable,disable,0,locked
    /synth_mode/loc,7700,enable,(38100/usb),(lsb),10.0,CW,external,10,enable,disable,0,locked
    /synth_mode/lod,7700,enable,(38100/usb),(lsb),10.0,CW,external,10,enable,disable,0,locked
    /synth_mode/loe,7700,enable,(92400/lsb),(lsb),10.0,CW,external,10,enable,disable,0,locked
    /synth_mode/lof,7700,enable,(92400/lsb),(lsb),10.0,CW,external,10,enable,disable,0,locked

  There are a few things to note here:

   . There is only one line in dbbc3_synth' for each external-LO instead of a
     separate line for each IF (LO). The one line for each external-LO will
     match both polarizations. This simplifies what is needed and helps save
     space in the 'ext_lo' internal table, which can support 40 entries total.

   . If you want the 'synth_mode=...' commands to set the synthesizers as
     opposed to just checking them, replace the 'synth_mode' commands with:

       synth_mode=
       synth_mode=loa,,,force
       synth_mode=lob,,,force
       synth_mode=loc,,,force
       synth_mode=lod,,,force
       synth_mode=loe,,,force
       synth_mode=lof,,,force
       synth_mode=loa,,,check
       synth_mode=lob,,,check
       synth_mode=loc,,,check
       synth_mode=lod,,,check
       synth_mode=loe,,,check
       synth_mode=lof,,,check

     That will both set and check the synthesizers.

   . If your station has eight IFs, you could include the corresponding
     'synth_mode=...' commands for the additional IFs ('log' and 'loh'). That
     will cover all possible IFs. If there is no LO defined for an IF, the
     command becomes a no-op.

   . Although this example just gives the relevant external-LO ('ext_lo=...')
     for these LOs ('lo=...'). It is recommended to include external-LOs for
     all other receivers. This allows the 'dbbc3_synth' procedure to be mode
     independent. The correct external-LO is selected using the net-LO
     frequency range and side-band that it is specified for. For example, to
     also cover external USB LOs for geodetic S/X, you might use:

       ext_lo=
       ext_lo=all,2020,usb,2020,,usb
       ext_lo=all,8080,usb,8080,,usb
       ext_lo=all,20400,usb,20400,,usb
       ext_lo=all,38100,usb,45800,,lsb
       ext_lo=all,92400,lsb,84700,,usb
